3. Data derived into floodq/geodata.py, floodq/shapes.py and floodq/roads.py
   (and the saved runs in offline_data.js):

   * Roads, rivers and lakes: Natural Earth 1:10m (naturalearthdata.com), public domain.
   * Sea depth and broad inland relief: ETOPO1 at 10 arc-minutes, NOAA National
     Centers for Environmental Information (doi:10.7289/V5C8276M), public domain,
     as packaged by the Fatiando a Terra project.
   * Land and water: GLOBE 1 km land mask (NOAA), public domain, read with the
     global-land-mask package (MIT).
   * Town names and populations: GeoNames (geonames.org), CC BY 4.0, read with
     the geonamescache package (MIT). Contains data from GeoNames.
   * County populations: US Census Bureau 2019 estimates as listed in the
     UID_ISO_FIPS lookup table of the COVID-19 Data Repository by the Center for
     Systems Science and Engineering at Johns Hopkins University, CC BY 4.0.

4. Map tiles and live layers are not stored in this repository. They load at
   run time from their publishers (USGS The National Map, NOAA via the
   University of Florida GeoPlan Center, FEMA, AWS Terrain Tiles / USGS 3DEP,
   Florida Division of Emergency Management), whose attributions appear on the map.
